  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: **Second Number = (First Number × 2) + 1**\n\n**Third Number = (Second Number × 2) + 1**\n\n**(46, 93, 187):**\n\n⇒ 93 = (46 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 93 = 92 + 1\n\n→ 93 = 93\n\n⇒ 187 = (93 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 187 = 187.\n\n**(123, 247, 495):**\n\n⇒ 247 = (123 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 247 = 246 + 1\n\n→ 247 = 247\n\n⇒ 495 = (247 × 2) + 1 \n\n→ 495 = 294 + 1\n\n→ 495 = 495.\n\nLet's check each option as per the logic:\n\n**1) (208, 418, 837):**\n\n⇒ 418 = (208 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 418 = 416 + 1\n\n→ **418 ≠ 417** → Doesn't follow the logic.\n\n**2) (313, 627, 1255):**\n\n⇒ 627 = (313 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 627 = 626 + 1\n\n→ 627 = 627\n\n⇒ 1255 = (627 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 1255 = 1254 + 1\n\n→ **1255 = 1255 **⇒ Follow the logic.\n\n**3) (111, 213, 427):**\n\n⇒ 213 = (111 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 213 = 222 + 1\n\n→ 213 ≠ 223 ⇒ Doesn't follow the logic.\n\n**4) (184, 369, 729):**\n\n⇒ 369 = (184 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 369 = 368 + 1\n\n→ 369 = 369\n\n⇒ 729 = (369 × 2) + 1\n\n→ 729 = 738 + 1\n\n→ 729 ≠ 739 ⇒ Doesn't follow the logic.\n\nHere, we can see that only Option 2 follow the logic.\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\" (313, 627, 1255) \"**.",
